00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:35.360
If you're hungry, eat up!

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:44.740
After finally reuniting with Birk underneath the castle, Ronja saw that he'd grown thin from hunger.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:54.170
Every morning throughout the long winter, she secretly delivered food to her brother.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:02:01.680
This kept him and Borka's robbers alive.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:09.270
Lousy Robbers

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:09.270
Lousy Robbers

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:06.910
Undis is amazed every morning because there are still a few peas and a little flour left.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:13.250
She assumes this sorcery must be the wild harpies' doing.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.250
Yup.

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:23.550
Perhaps she might be right about that.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:24.630
Eh?

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:30.850
You do look a bit like a little harpy,

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.100
Ronja.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:37.350
Oh, but I'm much nicer than a harpy,

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.020
and I don't have claws.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.740
Yup, you're as nice as nice can be.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.200
How many times do you plan to save my life,

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.700
my sister?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:59.670
As many times as you've saved mine!

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:00.940
The fact is,

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:04.800
we can't manage without each other anymore, right?

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.880
I realize that now!

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:12.890
That's true. So Mattis and Borka can think what they like.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.690
Hey, Birk! Have you eaten enough?

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:27.030
Yup.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.540
Then next is...

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:04.070
I'm already so completely deloused...

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:09.110
I think you're just combing my hair in vain.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.910
Whether or not that's true, we shall see.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.540
Ow-ow-ow...

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.420
Ow!

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.300
But, can't you—be more gentle?

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.680
You'll comb out my hair too!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:53.370
Gradually the harsh winter began to turn milder.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:56.790
The snow melted little by little.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.710
One day mid-thaw...

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:20.180
Help me!

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.600
Nooo!

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:24.190
Spare me!

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.980
Stop it!

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:28.780
Lovis! Stop this!

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.070
For God's sake!

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.700
This is tyranny!

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.490
How pitiful!

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:34.450
Yes!

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:37.870
Lovis, such things are harmful to our health.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.490
You should stop this.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:40.700
He's right!

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.160
Well said! Fjosok!

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:44.240
He's absolutely right!

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:44.790
Yeah!

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:45.960
No objection!

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.380
I don't want to catch cold!

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:50.670
Is that all you have to say?

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.550
Wh-What in the name of all the wild harpies?!

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:56.430
We'll all catch cold!

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:58.140
For sure!

00:06:58.140 --> 00:06:59.100
Yeah!

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.430
That's right!

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:05.190
Sturkus, you take off that headband too.

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:12.400
M-My late grandmother said never to take this off...

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:19.410
You guys too! Take off everything you're wearing on your heads.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.830
I can't wash it like that!

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.080
Jutis!

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.170
Joen! Pelie!

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:27.210
I can't, I can't...

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:31.880
Lovis, I can't. I just can't do it.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:34.260
It'd be unthinkable to take this off...

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.050
How terrible!

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:38.510
There's no way I could do it.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.850
Give me a break!

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.270
Don't cry, Pelie!

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:50.570
The smell of winter must go now,
even if every robber perishes in the process.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.280
Get it through your heads!

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:25.810
Mom, I'm ready.

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:27.230
Thank you.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:41.080
Ronja, you'll help me, right?

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.990
Yeah, of course.

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:53.750
It's cold!

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.920
Cold, cold, cold!

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.150
It's really cold!

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.930
As I thought, this isn't healthy...

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:14.020
Damn it! Lovis!

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:19.200
Lovis! She's even worse than the wild harpies!

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:23.160
What is the "smell of winter"?! That nonsense can go to hell!

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:31.120
Damn you, Lovis, we'll remember this!

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:34.460
Worthless wench!

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:35.710
Rotten saltfish!

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:37.380
Now I'm desperate!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.050
Damn you! Damnit!

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.590
The festival of despair!

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:41.800
Really...

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:43.260
Dull-witted!

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:47.220
Dimly dull-witted!

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:53.860
That was hilarious.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:59.070
Lovis' strictness is beyond words.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:00.200
Oh?

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:10.290
Like bandits, they stripped{hehe} them of all their possessions!

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:33.060
Skalle-Per.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:38.190
Are you going to welcome the spring without removing that muddy dirt?

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:45.200
Do you want this old man tumbling around in the snow naked?

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:50.500
I may die anyway...

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:59.380
But Lovis, I want to do it with the dirt I've got on me.

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:07.100
Fine. Do as you like.

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:11.100
But before you do,

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:15.520
could you at least tidy up the wool of those other sheep?

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:19.690
Yeah, I'd be glad to.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:28.910
But I'm going to spare my own little tufts of hair.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:34.580
I'll soon be under the ground, after all.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.390
You stop that about dying!

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:49.680
I haven't lived a day of my earthly life without you yet, you old fool!

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:56.560
So you can't just go and die behind my back!

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.520
Remember that!

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:05.570
We shall see, little boy.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.020
Mommy!

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:21.060
Fjosok?

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:33.620
Hey, come quick!

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:48.260
Boss...

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:55.080
Hey!

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:17.370
You guys, those really suit you.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:20.410
Most of those garments my grandfather stole in his time.

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:25.500
It seems all the men's clothing was already gone when they came looking.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:59.870
Now everyone. Let's make peace.

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:12.300
Th-This is...

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:15.540
Chicken soup!

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:17.850
Yeah!

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:19.850
Lovis outdid herself!

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:22.350
She's so great! She understands us!

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:24.190
What a wonderful smell!

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:24.850
Yeah!

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:16.900
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:16.900
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:53.510
At last our splendid robber life begins again!

00:16:54.190 --> 00:16:56.990
Yeah, my body is itching all over!

00:16:58.070 --> 00:16:59.490
You guys!

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:03.120
We're not going out to play, okay?

00:17:03.530 --> 00:17:08.080
Mattis' Robbers came from my grandfather, my great-grandfather,

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:11.380
my great-great-grandfather... 
Like this, it has descended through generations...

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.000
Daddy!

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:17.210
Wait, Daddy!

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.260
Daddy!

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.310
It's today!

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:31.650
Today's the day I can go into the forest, isn't it?

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:36.440
Yeah, I did promise:

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:41.950
When we started heading back into the forest, you could go out too.

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:43.740
Yeah, that's right!

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:47.100
You said the spring forests were full of danger,

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:50.580
and I couldn't go until it was time for your robbers to set out.

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:54.000
But now, it's that time of year!

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:55.250
Is that right?

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:01.720
Off you go then.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:02.540
Yup.

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:04.550
But still...

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:12.900
Don't slip and drown yourself in some treacherous little melt pool.

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:17.020
And if I do?

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:27.910
Now after being cooped up all winter,
 you'll have something to make a fuss about at last.

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:34.670
My Ronja.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:51.840
Let's go!

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:52.520
Heyah!

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:51.120
Wondrous smells!

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:07.050
Lovely sounds!

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.030
It's been so long!

00:21:44.270 --> 00:21:46.190
Birk!

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:52.240
I've been waiting a long time!

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:49.380
I have to shout out a spring scream...

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:51.380
If I don't, I'll...

00:22:51.380 --> 00:22:52.800
...burst!

00:22:54.800 --> 00:22:57.640
Listen. You can hear the spring, right?

00:23:07.690 --> 00:23:10.400
Spring came to the forest.

00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:13.240
A spring of new life.

